  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2024 Afghanistan Herat Earthquake</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multiple earthquakes struck western Afghanistan on Saturday between 11am-12 local time, with the first and largest at a magnitude of 6.3, according to U.S. Geological Survey (USGS). Some humanitarian impacted is expected. NS collecting information, according to initial unverified information from ARCS there are five deaths and 30 injuries around Zinda Jan.
The earthquake&#x2019;s epicentre was in Zinda Jan, 40 km northwest of Herat.  As of now, no official reports of casualties. However, some structural damages to houses and buildings have been observed in certain areas. 
In Herat City, hundreds of people left their homes and workplaces, and headed to the streets.
According to preliminary information from ARCS, there are five deaths and 100 injuries around Zinda Jan, but this is yet to be verified with the authorities. ARCS has activated their emergency operations centre to monitor and closely coordinate the response . IFRC is coordinating with PNS in the country as well as with ANDMA , the national disaster management agency. 
According to initial findings of the assessment the authorities, 2,445 people died, with a further 9,240 people injured. Partners and local authorities anticipate the number of casualties to increase as search and rescue efforts continue amid reports that some people may be trapped under collapsed buildings.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is to provide 300K support to Afghanistan covering the Herat Earthquake and the migration crisis.</narrative>
  </description>
